SUMMARY:The Human Condition I: No Greater Love
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, 2155 Center St\, Berkeley\, CA 94704
DESCRIPTION:Masaki Kobayashi’s three-part antiwar masterpiece follows the
  awakening—and disillusionment—of a Japanese soldier (the great Tatsuy
 a Nakadai) during World War II. “Amazingly powerful in its emotional swe
 ep and the depth of its historical insight. . . . Kobayashi’s monumental
  film can clarify and enrich your understanding of what it is to be alive
 ” (New York Times).\nhttps://bampfa.org/event/human-condition-no-greater
 -love\nFrom Pushpin Bay Area: https://pushpin.city/bayarea/
URL:https://bampfa.org/event/human-condition-no-greater-love
END:VEVENT
